### 1. Identified External Dependencies

Before refactoring, [`FleetCoreEngine`](https://github.com/jeremiahjmorris1126-coder/TRUCKWITHEASE-1/blob/main/server/fleetCore.ts) and the associated route handlers had direct coupling to several static calls, system environments, and hardware resources:

1. **Time / System Clock**: Direct static calls to `Date.now()` and `new Date().toISOString()`, preventing deterministic time-travel or deterministic token/audit test assertions.
2. **Entropy / Randomness / ID Generation**: Direct static calls to `Math.random()` and ad-hoc string formatting for driver IDs, tokens, audit IDs, and PINs.
3. **Data Stores / State (DB/Repository)**: Internal instantiation of `new Map()` with hardcoded seed data directly inside the constructor, preventing external database integration or lightweight test doubles.
4. **Hardware Telemetry Provider (Traxxas & J1939 ECU)**: In-memory simulation and static baud rate/latency assumptions coupled inside the engine.
5. **Static Configuration & Environmental Constants**: Hardcoded default driver IDs, vehicle dimensions (13' 6"), and FMCSA compliance defaults.

---

### 2. Introduced Abstractions & Interfaces

We introduced clean interfaces in [`server/fleetCore.ts`](https://github.com/jeremiahjmorris1126-coder/TRUCKWITHEASE-1/blob/main/server/fleetCore.ts):

```typescript
// System Clock Abstraction
export interface IClock {
  now(): number;
  toISOString(): string;
}

// Randomness & Identifier Generation Abstraction
export interface IRandomGenerator {
  random(): number;
  generateDriverId(name: string): string;
  generatePin(): string;
  generateTransponderId(): string;
  generateToken(driverId: string, timestamp: number): string;
  generateAuditId(timestamp: number): string;
}

// Driver Storage Repository
export interface IDriverRepository {
  getAll(): DriverAuthRecord[];
  getById(id: string): DriverAuthRecord | undefined;
  findByIdentifier(identifier: string): DriverAuthRecord | undefined;
  save(driver: DriverAuthRecord): void;
  count(): number;
}

// Modular Function & Feature Repository
export interface IFunctionCatalogRepository {
  getAll(): AppFunctionDefinition[];
  getById(id: string): AppFunctionDefinition | undefined;
  updateToggles(toggles: Record<string, boolean>): {
    activeFunctions: string[];
    disabledFunctions: string[];
  };
}

// Highway Restriction Engine (HRE) Route Repository
export interface IHreRestrictionRepository {
  getAll(): HreRestrictionRecord[];
  findByCorridor(corridor?: string): HreRestrictionRecord[];
}

// Traxxas Telemetry Provider
export interface ITraxxasTelemetryProvider {
  getTelemetry(jitter?: { speedDelta: number; rpmDelta: number; shock: number }): TraxxasTelemetryRecord;
  pushTelemetry(frame: Partial<TraxxasTelemetryRecord>, timestamp: string): TraxxasTelemetryRecord;
  ping(transponderId?: string, timestamp?: string, latencyMs?: number): TraxxasPingResponse;
  setTransponderId(id: string): void;
}

// Fleet Configuration Options
export interface IFleetConfiguration {
  defaultDriverId: string;
  standardTruckHeightFt: number;
  j1939BaudRateKbps: number;
  telemetrySamplingRateHz: number;
  defaultCarrierName: string;
  defaultUsdotNumber: string;
}
```

---

### 3. Constructor Injection & DI Container

All dependencies are injected via constructor in [`FleetCoreEngine`](https://github.com/jeremiahjmorris1126-coder/TRUCKWITHEASE-1/blob/main/server/fleetCore.ts#L440-L460):

```typescript
export interface FleetCoreDependencies {
  clock: IClock;
  random: IRandomGenerator;
  driverRepo: IDriverRepository;
  functionRepo: IFunctionCatalogRepository;
  hreRepo: IHreRestrictionRepository;
  telemetryProvider: ITraxxasTelemetryProvider;
  config: IFleetConfiguration;
}

export class FleetCoreEngine {
  private activeDriverId: string;

  constructor(private readonly deps: FleetCoreDependencies) {
    this.activeDriverId = deps.config.defaultDriverId;
  }

  // Public methods consume this.deps.clock, this.deps.driverRepo, this.deps.random, etc.
}
```

A DI container ([`FleetCoreContainer`](https://github.com/jeremiahjmorris1126-coder/TRUCKWITHEASE-1/blob/main/server/fleetCore.ts#L650-L685)) and factory function `createFleetCore()` manage dependency resolution with production defaults ([`SystemClock`](https://github.com/jeremiahjmorris1126-coder/TRUCKWITHEASE-1/blob/main/server/fleetCore.ts#L270-L278), [`DefaultRandomGenerator`](https://github.com/jeremiahjmorris1126-coder/TRUCKWITHEASE-1/blob/main/server/fleetCore.ts#L280-L310), in-memory repositories). The default singleton instance `fleetCore` preserves the exact public API for [server.ts](https://github.com/jeremiahjmorris1126-coder/TRUCKWITHEASE-1/blob/main/server.ts).

---

### 4. How to Unit Test the Main Flow

Because all dependencies are explicit interfaces, you can test the driver sign-up, sign-in, and HRE/Traxxas audit flows without timers, external systems, or flakiness:

```typescript
import test from 'node:test';
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { FleetCoreEngine } from '../server/fleetCore';

// 1. Create lightweight test doubles for IClock and IRandomGenerator
class FakeClock {
  now() { return 1793462400000; }
  toISOString() { return '2026-10-31T16:00:00.000Z'; }
}

class FakeRandom {
  random() { return 0.5; }
  generateDriverId(name) { return `drv-test-${name.toLowerCase()}`; }
  generatePin() { return '1234'; }
  generateTransponderId() { return 'TRAXXAS-TEST-01'; }
  generateToken(id, ts) { return `tok_test_${id}_${ts}`; }
  generateAuditId(ts) { return `audit-${ts}`; }
}

// 2. Instantiate FleetCoreEngine with mocks
const clock = new FakeClock();
const random = new FakeRandom();
const engine = new FleetCoreEngine({
  clock,
  random,
  driverRepo: new InMemoryDriverRepository([]),
  functionRepo: new InMemoryFunctionCatalogRepository(),
  hreRepo: new InMemoryHreRestrictionRepository(),
  telemetryProvider: new InMemoryTraxxasTelemetryProvider(clock),
  config: { ...DEFAULT_FLEET_CONFIG, defaultDriverId: 'drv-test-initial' },
});

// 3. Test the main registration & sign-in flow
test('enrolling driver produces deterministic ID, timestamp, and token', () => {
  const result = engine.signupDriver({
    name: 'Marcus Ortiz',
    cdlNumber: 'TX-CDL-8819204',
  });

  assert.equal(result.driver.driverId, 'drv-test-marcus ortiz');
  assert.equal(result.driver.createdAt, '2026-10-31T16:00:00.000Z');
  assert.equal(result.token, 'tok_test_drv-test-marcus ortiz_1793462400000');
  assert.equal(result.driver.fmcsaPin, '1234');
});
```

All 13 test suites in [`tests/cockpit.test.js`](https://github.com/jeremiahjmorris1126-coder/TRUCKWITHEASE-1/blob/main/tests/cockpit.test.js) and the full production build (`npm run build`) pass without errors. All changes are saved.
